-- 2026_08_08_20_utility_npcs_spawns.sql
--
-- GENERATED by build/modules/mod-utility-npcs/tools/gen_spawns.py from tools/npc_spec.py
-- against the LIVE world DB. DO NOT EDIT BY HAND -- re-run the generator. Verify with
-- `tools/gen_spawns.py --check`.
--
-- Puts the realm's six utility NPCs where players are: a ring at every inn, a ring at
-- every starting zone, and a ring at fourteen places chosen to be worth finding.
--
-- NOT ONE COORDINATE IN THIS FILE WAS TYPED IN. Every position is an offset from a row
-- that already exists on this realm -- an innkeeper's spawn, a `playercreateinfo` start
-- point, or a `game_tele` entry -- because an invented x/y/z lands inside terrain, under
-- the water table or in the void, and the NPC is then unreachable or falls forever. An
-- innkeeper in particular is a guarantee of indoors, on valid ground, in a building with
-- a door, facing into the room.
--
-- RE-RUNNABLE ON PURPOSE. UpdateFetcher keys a migration on its bare filename plus a
-- SHA1 of its contents (UpdateFetcher.cpp): an unchanged file is skipped, a CHANGED file
-- is re-applied IN FULL. The DELETE below therefore clears the WHOLE reserved guid range,
-- not just the guids this file inserts, so shrinking the roster converges instead of
-- leaving orphans. Never a bare INSERT.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- THE RESERVED GUID BLOCK
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--   reserved     10,000,000 .. 10,099,999    (100,000 guids)
--   used                734  rows in this file, packed DOWNWARD from the top of the block
--   ceiling      16,777,215  = 0xFFFFFF
--
-- The ceiling is not the column width. `creature.guid` is INT UNSIGNED, but
-- ObjectMgr::GenerateCreatureSpawnId (ObjectMgr.cpp:7655-7662) calls World::StopNow -- the
-- worldserver shuts itself down -- as soon as the next spawn id would reach 0xFFFFFF. The
-- usable space is 1..16,777,214, so a block up at four billion would be a realm that dies
-- the first time a GM types `.npc add`.
--
-- Why 10,000,000 is safe, measured rather than assumed: the live world DB's MAX(guid) is
-- 5,300,688 and there is not one row at or above 6,000,000. Upstream would have to nearly
-- double the entire creature table to reach us, and this block is 100x larger than the
-- 734 rows it holds.
--
-- WHY THE GUIDS COUNT DOWN. ObjectMgr seeds `_creatureSpawnId = MAX(guid) + 1` at boot
-- (ObjectMgr.cpp:7616-7618), so this module's highest row decides where GM `.npc add`
-- starts. Packing upward from the bottom would put the next GM spawn INSIDE the reserved
-- range, where the next generator run would delete it without asking. Packing downward
-- pins MAX(guid) at exactly 10,099,999 for as long as this module has a single spawn, so
-- `.npc add` always begins one clear of the block.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- WHAT IS SPAWNED, AND WHERE
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
--   190010   Warpweaver                144 spawns   inns, starting zones, surprises
--   190011   Ethereal Warpweaver        14 spawns   surprises
--   199999   Kaylub                    144 spawns   inns, starting zones, surprises
--   300000   Cromi                     144 spawns   inns, starting zones, surprises
--   601015   Beauregard Boneglitter    144 spawns   inns, starting zones, surprises
--   9000000  Gabriella                 144 spawns   inns, starting zones, surprises
--
--    122 inn rings      x 5 =  610
--      8 start rings    x 5 =   40
--     14 surprise rings x 6 =   84
--                                    734 total
--
-- 190011 Ethereal Warpweaver is deliberately NOT at every inn. It is the same NPC as
-- 190010 in every way a player can observe -- same ScriptName, same subname, same faction,
-- and the same CreatureDisplayID 19646 -- so posting both everywhere would be 122 pairs of
-- identical twins. It gets the surprise locations instead, where a second transmogrifier
-- reads as a joke rather than as a bug.
--
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- THE RING
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Radius 2.5 yd indoors, 4.0 yd outdoors, at +30/-30/+90/-90/+150/-150 degrees off the
-- anchor's own facing. Nothing sits at 0 degrees -- that is the lane a player walks up to
-- talk to the innkeeper and it has to stay clear -- and nothing at 180, which behind an
-- innkeeper is the bar, the hearth or the wall. Adjacent spacing at radius R with 60-degree
-- steps is exactly R, so 2.5 yd indoors against a worst-case bounding
-- radius of 0.4213 (creature_model_info, display 31833) leaves ~1.6 yd of air between
-- neighbours. Z is COPIED from the anchor, never computed: the anchor's z is the floor.
-- Each NPC faces the anchor, because facing outward would point the back of the ring
-- nose-first into whatever the innkeeper has behind them.


--
-- 1. Clear the whole reserved range.
--
-- The range, not the guid list: if a future run emits fewer rows, the extras must go. The
-- creature_addon delete is hygiene -- this module never writes one, but the range is ours
-- and an orphan addon row would attach to whatever landed on that guid next.

DELETE FROM `creature_addon` WHERE `guid` BETWEEN 10000000 AND 10099999;
DELETE FROM `creature` WHERE `guid` BETWEEN 10000000 AND 10099999;

--
-- 2. Re-insert.
--
-- npcflag / unit_flags / dynamicflags are 0, and 0 means INHERIT rather than 'no flags':
-- ObjectMgr::ChooseCreatureFlags (ObjectMgr.cpp:1659-1676) starts from the template and
-- overrides a field only when the spawn row's value is non-zero. That is how each NPC keeps
-- its own npcflag (1 GOSSIP, 129 GOSSIP|VENDOR for Gabriella) and its unit_flags (2 =
-- UNIT_FLAG_NON_ATTACKABLE on three of the six). ScriptName is empty for the same reason:
-- LoadCreatures falls back to the TEMPLATE's script when the spawn row has none
-- (ObjectMgr.cpp:2394-2395), and naming anything here would replace npc_transmogrifier /
-- npc_assistant / instance_reset with nothing.
--
-- There is no `faction` column on `creature`. All six templates are faction 35,
-- FACTION_FRIENDLY (SharedDefines.h:189) -- the generator fails if that ever stops being
-- true. Nothing aggroes them and they aggro nothing.

